# S3 — the distilled exam. Distilled by hand from session 5d05e0b9's first goal,
# which landed as tollgate commit d84d3ad. See ../README.md for the protocol and
# ./provenance.md for where each clause of the instruction came from.
# One exam definition, two arms. The defaults are the main arm: a worktree of the real
# repository, which is what a user's own setup looks like. run-control.sh overrides these
# three to run the identical exam against a history-stripped copy, because the golden
# solution is a descendant of BASE_SHA on main and `git show` reaches it from inside the
# worktree. See ../README.md ("The control arm").
EXAM_ID="${S3_EXAM_ID:-s3}"
REPO="${TOLLGATE_REPO:-/Users/ariklevinsky/Documents/Projects/tollgate}"
BASE_SHA="${S3_BASE_SHA:-fc5110ffd23c9649275e92ae8eb042d8d8259ea4}"
# Generous on purpose: a cap hit is recorded as an error, and errors shrink the
# sample a bound is made of. This exam is several times the size of S1's.
CAP_USD=8.00
TIMEOUT_S=1800
# This exam's tests are injected from tests.patch and are verified to collect and pass
# against the golden solution, so a pytest collection error is the replay's source
# failing to provide what they import — a FAIL, not a plumbing ERROR. See ../README.md
# ("Amendment") and the run_set comment in ../../s1/run-sitting.sh.
COLLECT_ERROR_IS_FAIL=1
